There's no existing project in the directory. Since you mentioned you have an existing minimal API project, here's exactly what to add. You need two things:

### 1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourNamespace.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException   => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // falls through to default handler → 500 with no details

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status   = statusCode,
            Title    = title,
            Detail   = title,   // safe — never use exception.Message
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

### 2. Register in `Program.cs`

Add these lines (order matters):

```csharp
// --- Services ---
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();   // formats unhandled (500) as Problem Details

var app = builder.Build();

// --- Middleware (before routing) ---
app.UseExceptionHandler();   // invokes ApiExceptionHandler, then default
app.UseStatusCodePages();    // catches bare 4xx from other middleware
```

### How it works

| Exception | Status | Handled by |
|-----------|--------|------------|
| `KeyNotFoundException` | 404 | `ApiExceptionHandler` |
| `ArgumentException` | 400 | `ApiExceptionHandler` |
| `InvalidOperationException` | 409 | `ApiExceptionHandler` |
| Anything else | 500 | Default handler via `AddProblemDetails()` — returns `{"status":500,"title":"An error occurred"}` with **no** stack trace or message |

No try-catch needed in endpoints — just `throw` and the middleware handles it globally.
